[{"id":"VRCE-7-75-1","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":75,"verse":1,"english":"After the conversation between Råma and Bharata had been over, Laksmana, with reasonable words, said to the former.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-84-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7075001","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5d5c12ae7d7724d690915c6f3bc3d362b3603359509620a2e9495ba709078cad","compact":"28530580df0cd054fa8f1aa519ff1bf944ec545464a4d1986913db547be35ca4","nasal":"593672ec37a2248c8c1b2b9fa3f84af7053e100c3e7044859f2f10fe7b4d7e30"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-75-2","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":75,"verse":2,"english":"O Rāma, among sacrifices Aśvamedha is the best and the remover of all sins; it is my prayer therefore that your desire might be turned towards this great and highly purifying sacrifice.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.82,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-84-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7075002","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"deb710c212a21e1e4f54288e3aba2f4eb00e62218f184bc800d3e66a9758a62e","compact":"228640f0a1d52f6c8403d520eb71342fc6d2d47f0921221793de9e3572eba1ba","nasal":"65fa2c0f18036bc160de7749c5bebccc78e04c6143a7b5a934c75d1c1ba03212"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-75-3","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":75,"verse":3,"english":"It is said in this Purānas, that Purandara, sullied by the sin consequent upon slaying a Brāhmaṇa, was again purified by celebrating a horse sacrifice.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-84-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7075003","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"615209e6eafe0f7ec1bfc24ceffbebdfba328cee9b3e20902936ece33c43bb42","compact":"a7f9b6bf1a6a5adca9577cd602892c9210d098ede10a1d3745e3324228f8220c","nasal":"a7f9b6bf1a6a5adca9577cd602892c9210d098ede10a1d3745e3324228f8220c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-75-4","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":75,"verse":4,"english":"O you having long arms, formerly, during the war between gods and demons there flourished a highly honoured Asura under the name of Vſtra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.788,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-84-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7075004","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"017d899e8ea0dc6034f164e49c4279906d1b23108793dd6626b6cd15b681f001","compact":"b6c349c0fe2b7a15cba7925df063d0e03fdb0666735d351dd201c2be1a7d4280","nasal":"b6c349c0fe2b7a15cba7925df063d0e03fdb0666735d351dd201c2be1a7d4280"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-75-5","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":75,"verse":5,"english":"The breadth of his body was a hundred Yojanas and the height there of was three hundred Yojanas. Considering all under his subjection he used to regard them with affection.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.764,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-84-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7075005","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c96a7dbbe2b8995cf59703d199b8d9f6faa8fd2677e3ff391ae4e5e1f0b12043","compact":"0508905e4ce6743256a8ecb3c1a5f6fc439c31c7c79d4935e0deae776a9d1d0f","nasal":"0508905e4ce6743256a8ecb3c1a5f6fc439c31c7c79d4935e0deae776a9d1d0f"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-75-6","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":75,"verse":6,"english":"He was pious, grateful and used to perform nothing without proper deliberation. And treading tracks he used to govern his subjects very carefully.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.844,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-84-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7075006","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7f6d5f9d1992c85dfcf9c4902f0a7b5e0f0e107c9d09278a2afad4725f7638c7","compact":"be0f04ca925e5ebe597c9762c7a38aeec013fb58a9e38ab19ad54a901453462f","nasal":"be0f04ca925e5ebe597c9762c7a38aeec013fb58a9e38ab19ad54a901453462f"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-75-7","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":75,"verse":7,"english":"During his administration earth produced all wished-for objects; roots and fruits were tasteful and flowers were fragrant.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.704,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-84-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7075007","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1197ae85f7e300cd2ef3a952e501ca5c61818e769fd673dfdd67945d4ff5086f","compact":"cb639099b145fa0fbe69a1934ecafd51d2c1b6d3d8516afb019406ae1076267f","nasal":"443ea4252cb36190310fbef106da3de72cd0b223e9757e6e1cf1e2642133bc91"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-75-8","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":75,"verse":8,"english":"Without being cultivated earth used to yield crops. In this wise for many long years he governed a prosperous and wonderful kingdom.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-84-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7075008","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"92aa9086c2b771245ddad20c360e9bfd659daa456e8ff41953fef1713daed233","compact":"445866b3b688dd881f47701b059d20baa917f6bed1f6e5922ca8ad53fc9c982f","nasal":"65cb46f1ed6a2ef8509d9cec3605d2fab553ebe14f5650cc04e76dc885e9829d"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-75-9","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":75,"verse":9,"english":"Thereupon he determined upon performing a hard penance. He considered asceticism as the best of all and regarded all other things as mere illusions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-84-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7075009","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e12709636e9bc323582f6046c7acd4407a9818e23b7a8cc46698700beba5be21","compact":"f4b5e15749b41e3a11223a36e07267196f2e839514171d14d4c955e50cc4d347","nasal":"27b44ae67c4c59ffd53c06355b2a7a47cf10707b5304bbf381dc96cf55779779"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-75-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":75,"verse":10,"english":"Having resolved thus and placed his son Madhureśvara on the throne Vſtra engaged in austerities creating terror to all deities.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.688,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-84-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7075010","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"db873aca4bab509559f1432134178322b1eb2e4e70dd1a2df947d8162f9f5720","compact":"f1a2a46e8bdb8b7e4313c57273e984798fb87ea291a3e81e5b5da515696cdfbb","nasal":"f1a2a46e8bdb8b7e4313c57273e984798fb87ea291a3e81e5b5da515696cdfbb"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-75-11","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":75,"verse":11,"english":"He being thus engaged in asceticism, Indra, greatly terrified, approached Vişņu and said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-84-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7075011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f7dd243b19475fadb8acd446f8af37d09d58c53a4cffd0b7fb9c78e8d783a132","compact":"c8811efe81457450714f67e0c3444eca237ca8ed947a9160ae06e7b08732eb3a","nasal":"c8811efe81457450714f67e0c3444eca237ca8ed947a9160ae06e7b08732eb3a"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-75-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":75,"verse":12,"english":"O you having long arms, by virtue of his asceticism Vſtra is about to conquer all the worlds. He is pious, so I cannot subdue him.","