rom the time he succeeded in propitiating you, he has obtained the sovereignty of the three worlds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-84-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7075015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"89fba1e3bac035e983fb10a933864f971c189772abf4202117aa30dee6be5f2e","compact":"ec89a092ce93eca75781fd409dbe38f1cd6c9e7c6e37da7109b58e1c308c2c55","nasal":"ec89a092ce93eca75781fd409dbe38f1cd6c9e7c6e37da7109b58e1c308c2c55"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-75-16","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":75,"verse":16,"english":"Do you, therefore, be propitiated now; save you none can free this world from thorns and bring it at rest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.591,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-84-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7075016","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6c8f57273c401a5dbcf529ed76653ed5829330ec3ae8c96f183d91f617e79443","compact":"f059058a445de23425997363e873105d54e3ffd497370bba2eba798c7ad8973f","nasal":"0f16427fe366aa74e2b56f5557bd34845d272a52929b2067a22cf4005aac947e"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-75-17","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":75,"verse":17,"english":"O Vişnu, all the deities are waiting for you; do you help them by slaying Vộtra. O you having a large mind, you are always the help of these high-souled deities. It is impossible for any one else to accomplish the present work. You are the refuge of the helpless.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.762,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-84-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7075017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"87da8287fbc127758c965f122561ace6c416e531589d913c4f76fd2d0d939c96","compact":"1e557542a87ae3b413c441e408349293d1513e60